# argued-fork — pattern
@id argued-fork  @kind pattern  @layer library  @author toine  @lang en

## summary
~ At one point the way splits. The player proposes, the carrier argues with reasons of her own, then decides; the player's proposal changes the argument, not the right to decide.

## roles
role chooser : character : who decides
role fork : station : where the way splits
role option* : station : the stations the fork leads to (attrs: line)

## principles
! $chooser always argues once before going, whatever is proposed.
~0.7 If the voice proposes nothing, $chooser asks once, then picks herself.

## rules
when said.matches(direction) once if at($fork) -> say($option.line) {argue}

## beats_hint
hint the fork sits in the middle beat; each option leads to a different ending family

## variations
variation blind : the carrier cannot see either option; the player must remember something seen earlier
